+- Moving a task requires manager rights in the task's current project (like
+  delete) and write rights in the destination project (`404` if the destination
+  is not readable or does not exist, `403` if the user is only a viewer there,
+  `409` if archived). The task keeps its ID, title, status and assignee. The
+  assignee must be a contributor or manager of the destination (`400` otherwise).
+  A contributor in the destination may only move unassigned tasks or tasks
+  assigned to themselves (`403`, as with creating a task). Moving to the same
+  project is `400`.
